 "notes": "Document has 2 pages. Page 1 = Semesters One-Six; page 2 = Semesters Seven-Eight, followed by the Graduation Requirements Summary table, numbered footnotes, Program Notes, University Requirements paragraph, the Codes legend, and the Disclaimer (all excluded from `sections` per instructions, but note page 2's underlying content stream is NOT in visual top-to-bottom order -- the disclaimer/summary/notes/codes text is interleaved oddly relative to the two semester tables in raw extraction; a naive text-order parser could easily misplace Semester Seven/Eight rows relative to that trailing material).\n\nHeader/major-name ambiguity: the page header reads, on separate lines, \"Major Map: Music\" / \"Bachelor of Music (B.M.)\" / \"Music Education-Choral Concentration\" / \"School of Music\" / \"Bulletin Year: 2020-2021\". There is no single schema field for \"concentration,\" so I used the most specific line, \"Music Education-Choral Concentration,\" as `major`. A parser keying off the literal \"Major Map:\" line would instead extract \"Music\" -- flagging so a disagreement here isn't scored as a parser bug.\n\nEvery data row also carries a \"Major GPA\" column (a bare \"*\" for MR-coded courses, blank otherwise) between Min. Grade and Code. The provided schema has no field for it, so it was dropped entirely; this is a real printed column, not something I overlooked.\n\nVerbatim footnote-fusion quirk: \"Secondary Applied Lessons4 (MUED \u2026)\" has a space before the parenthesis in Semesters One, Two, and Three, but Semester Four prints it with no space -- \"Secondary Applied Lessons4(MUED 356 or MUED 266)\". Transcribed exactly as printed in each case rather than normalizing; a parser that normalizes whitespace will disagree with this row and would be right to.\n\n\"Primary Applied Lessons3(MUSC \u2026)\" consistently has no space after the footnote digit in every semester it appears (One through Seven) -- transcribed verbatim throughout.\n\nTwo rows are two-line wraps joined with a single space per instructions: \"MUED 107 Classroom Instruments\" prerequisite (\"C or better in MUED 200 & 356\" + \"or instructor permission\") and the Semester Seven course-choice row \"EDRD 500 Content Area Literacy PK-12\" + \"or EDEX 581 Teaching Rdg, to Adol. with Disabilities\" (title only, no separate prerequisite text).\n\n`total_credits_required` (\"132\") was taken from the \"Minimum Total Hours\" cell of the Graduation Requirements Summary table -- that table itself is excluded from `sections`, but the total is a top-level program field per the schema.\n\nNo `college` value is printed anywhere on the map (only \"School of Music\"), so I left `college` null and put \"School of Music\" in `department`; a different convention may be intended elsewhere in this corpus.\n\nMUSC 100 Recital Class (0 credits, min grade S) appears in Semesters One through Five but is absent from Semester Six onward -- confirmed present in the source, not an omission on my part."
